  {
    "text": "Stitching-free high-NA EUV approaches achieve an edge placement error of <1 nm and a process window >5% exposure latitude for logic and DRAM layers.",
    "topic": "Yield feasibility quantification"
  },
  {
    "text": "Design-technology co-optimization studies confirm that SADP with high-NA EUV decomposes critical layers into non-stitching sub-layers for all industry-standard logic and DRAM layouts.",
    "topic": "SADP decomposition universality"
  },
  {
    "text": "Central obscuration illumination sources provide a depth-of-focus of >50 nm for half-pitch 28 nm features across the entire slit, enabling stitching-free imaging.",
    "topic": "Illumination DOF mitigation"
  },
  {
    "text": "Wafer-scale yield comparison between stitching-free high-NA EUV and DUV multi-patterning shows equivalent or lower defectivity for DRAM arrays.",
    "topic": "Yield comparison with DUV"
  }
]
